      <title>about</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/about/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/about/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;figure class=&#34;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;img-container&#34; style=&#34;--w: 5472; --h: 3648;&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; alt=&#34;Me&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/olivia.jpg&#34; width=&#34;5472&#34; height=&#34;3648&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;    &#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hi, I&amp;rsquo;m Olivia. At my core, I have deep passion for robotics engineering in all aspects - whether that falls within autonomy software, hardware integration, or sensors &amp;amp; electrical design. My current rabbit hole: sensors &amp;amp; autonomy software, and deep learning as it relates to robotics.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Over the course of my degree, I&amp;rsquo;ve done a little bit of everything, and I&amp;rsquo;m always open to chat. Hit me up about anything engineering - or, running a half-marathon, doing a triathlon (one day!), and classical music, just some of my recent interests! You can find me at &lt;a href=&#34;mailto:olivia.ye@uwaterloo.ca&#34;&gt;olivia.ye@uwaterloo.ca&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
